        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Marjolet',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Marjolet is an elegant two-player card game from southwest France, and the direct ancestor of Bezique and Pinochle. Played with a 32-card French deck, it combines trick-taking with melding, featuring the unique 'Marjolet' (trump Jack) that can be melded with different Queens. The game is known for its tactical depth despite simple rules.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Played in southwest France. The name 'Marjolet' refers to the trump Jack, which has special melding powers. It is the direct ancestor of Bezique and the grandparent of Pinochle.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 players, playing individually.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "32-card 'French deck' - remove all cards below 7 from standard deck. Ranking: Ace (high), 10, King, Queen, Jack, 9, 8, 7. Note: 10 is second-highest, right below Ace.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "32-card 'French deck' - remove all cards below 7 from standard deck. Ranking: Ace (high), 10, King, Queen, Jack, 9, 8, 7. Note: 10 is second-highest, right below Ace.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Deal 6 cards to each player. Turn one card up next to remaining deck (stock) to determine trump suit.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
